|~ What is declared under `::explanation`, the kind of what
   `explain` answers, the page `doc` reads for a value and the value
   itself: its verbs. ~|

:explanation/page
  |~~ The page of what the explanation explains: of a name its own, of
      a value the page of the kind it shows, of an error the page of its
      site; null for a declaration without one.
  ~~|
  ~(/page)

:explanation/page/ofAnErrorIsThePageOfItsRefusal
  |~~ The page of an error is the page of the refusal that raised it. ~~|
  ::law~("x" | add 1 !| explain | page | eq (::number/add/SubjectNotNumberError | doc))

:explanation/page/prose
  |~~ The page that explains the value, null for a name without one. ~~|
  #[::doc ::null]

:explanation/value
  |~~ The value the explanation explains; an error among them raised, as
      it arrived before `!|` opened it.
  ~~|
  ~(/value)

:explanation/value/isTheValueExplained
  |~~ The value is the one explained. ~~|
  ::law~(42 | explain | value | eq 42)

:explanation/value/keepsAnErrorRaised
  |~~ An error explained stays raised. ~~|
  ::law~("x" | add 1 !| explain | value !| type | eq ::number/add/SubjectNotNumberError)
